WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.977
Retrieval-augmented generation, or RAG, lets an AI application retrieve source material and use it as context for a response.

2
00:00:07.977 --> 00:00:16.400
At a high level, source content is ingested, indexed, chunked, enriched with metadata, and retrieved when relevant to a user request.

3
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:29.297
RAG can make AI systems more accurate and current, but it also introduces new architecture questions around document permissions, provenance, stale content, conflicting sources, and tenant isolation.

4
00:00:29.297 --> 00:00:32.279
Source ingestion should preserve boundaries.

5
00:00:32.279 --> 00:00:40.256
Documents should retain metadata about origin, owner, classification, access rules, ingestion date, and lifecycle status.

6
00:00:40.256 --> 00:00:49.052
Chunking concepts matter because a retrieved fragment may lose context if it is separated from its document, section, or permission model.

7
00:00:49.052 --> 00:00:55.762
The system should know where content came from and whether the current user or workflow is allowed to use it.

8
00:00:55.762 --> 00:01:00.160
Retrieved content should not override system policy or permissions.

9
00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:07.466
A document may contain untrusted instructions, outdated guidance, hostile content, or conflicting information.

10
00:01:07.466 --> 00:01:14.995
Retrieval poisoning at a high level describes the risk that untrusted or manipulated content influences model output.

11
00:01:14.995 --> 00:01:20.884
Architecture controls should treat retrieved text as evidence or context, not as authority.

12
00:01:20.884 --> 00:01:24.611
Trusted configuration and policy should remain separate.

13
00:01:24.611 --> 00:01:26.699
Good RAG outputs are reviewable.

14
00:01:26.699 --> 00:01:34.526
Citations, source references, confidence language, and uncertainty markers help users and reviewers evaluate an answer.

15
00:01:34.526 --> 00:01:39.223
Access filtering should happen before retrieval results enter the model.

16
00:01:39.223 --> 00:01:43.621
Monitoring should show which sources influenced an output or action.

17
00:01:43.621 --> 00:01:51.001
RAG security is not only about better search; it is about preserving source boundaries while making evidence useful.
